   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Someday You'll Call My Name** (2 other sources): Terry Barber sang lead vocals, with Sierra Hull, Michael Cleveland and Mark Lavengood also guesting; Terry Barber took lead vocals, joined by guests Sierra Hull, Michael Cleveland and Mark Lavengood [1][2]\n- **Little Cabin Home On The Hill** (1 other source): Last played 2025-06-19, an 84-show gap, with Barber, Hull, Cleveland and Lavengood sitting in [1]\n- **Meet Me At The Creek** (1 other source): Mike Devol played bass on this one, and Royal Masat was not on stage [3]\n- **Don't Lie** (1 review): Reviewer found the Don't Lie and Meet Me At The Creek sandwich wild [4]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Broken Doe**: rare: 4 archived performances [6]\n- **Train That Carried My Girl Away**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [6]\n- **With Body & Soul**: rare: 3 archived performances [6]\n- **Maiden's Prayer**: rare: 4 archived performances [6]\n- **Baltimore Johnny**: rare: 5 archived performances [6]\n- **Life To Go**: back after 187 archived shows (1359 days); rare: 3 archived performances [6]\n- **Someday You'll Call My Name**: rare: 5 archived performances [6]\n- **Little Cabin Home On The Hill**: back after 327 archived shows (2372 days); rare: 7 archived performances [6]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **Billy2026-08-29** (recommended): source not stated; 28 songs; 179 min; rated 5/5 by 1 [1]. Said about its sound: Reviewer says the recording sounds excellent [4]\n- **BMFS2026-08-29**: source not stated; 28 songs; 180 min; rated 5/5 by 1 [2]\n- **billystrings2026-08-29**: source not stated; 29 songs; 182 min [3]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- The show was at the Ionia Freak Fair, held at the Ionia County Fairgrounds [3]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **Billy2026-08-29**: taped by Tony DeStefanis; source: Schoeps mk22 > nbobs > mixpre6ii [1]. Also: Schoeps mk22 mics into nbobs, a Mixpre6ii recorder, Audacity, CDWE, then TLH, finished as FLAC8 [1]\n- **BMFS2026-08-29**: taped by Tony DeStefanis; source: Schoeps mk41 (DINa) > nbobs > mixpre6ii [2]. Also: Schoeps mk41 mics in a DINa setup, into nbobs, Mixpre6ii, Audacity, CDWE, then TLH as FLAC8 [2]\n- **billystrings2026-08-29**: taped by jb; source: AKG 414 [3]",
